requestFraming.description:
`buffered`, `bytes`, `sse`, `ndjson`, `json_array` or `websocket`.
HTTP bodies are reconstructed regardless of transport framing;
WebSocket messages retain their boundaries in the events.

nextCursorId.description:
The id of the same item. Two requests can share a millisecond, and a
timestamp-only cursor would either repeat them forever or skip them;
the pair is unique because ids are.

Output_RulePresetDto.description:
A named set of rewrite rules. `rules` is what `apply_rule_preset` writes;
it is the ordinary write shape, so a caller may edit the list first and
send it through `rewrite().replace_rules` itself.
